Found by Kabe, 2026-10-11. Only the MIT shader is taken. The repository ships no meshes or atlases, and
nothing else from creategamecharacters.com (its SDK, characters, hair meshes, style folders) is fetched or used.

Safety pass (read in full, 2026-10-11, before vendoring): plain ES module with no imports. The only network
paths are loadHairParams (fetch of a caller-supplied style URL + "/mh_materials.json") and loadHairAtlas
(TextureLoader on a caller-supplied URL). Photonic calls neither. It has no eval, Function constructor,
dynamic import, DOM or storage access, and no telemetry. The creategamecharacters.com URL appears only in
comments.

What Photonic uses (spikes/hair/shade.js): createHairMaterials() on the node (TSL) path only, with
`instanced: true`, so one material per tier serves every wearer through the per-instance swatch attributes
gccRootA, gccRootB and gccTip. Its passes are the opaque alpha-to-coverage pass and the blended fringe under
MSAA, with root-to-tip tone, per-strand seed brightness and roughness, and the anisotropic GGX lobe through
an anisotropy (tangent) map. The atlas Photonic paints in code (spikes/hair/atlas.js) speaks its compact
format: R coverage, G root-to-tip, B per-strand seed. Photonic's additions sit on top of the returned
materials (a lighting model per tier, per-strand greying and the force bend), never inside this file.
